-- title:
--   r-integrality of a norm-q local unit of an Eichler order
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$, a prime $q$ and the quaternion algebra $H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, and assume $q\neq 2$ together with the predicate `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q$ lies in $w$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $H$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders (orders being $\mathbb Z$-submodules containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated and spanning $H$ over $\mathbb Q$, maximal among such) with relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$, and assume $q\nmid N$; let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order containing $R$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq q$ and $v$ a height-one prime containing $r$. Let $\bar w\in H^\times$ have reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w)=q$, where $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-ax_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-bx_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+abx_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$. Assume that for every $w\neq v$ not containing $q$ the image of $\bar w$ in $(H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w)^\times$ lies in [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45), i.e. both it and its inverse lie in the additive subgroup generated by the $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ a $w$-adic integer; and that for every $w\neq v$ conjugation by this image preserves membership in the local boxes of $R$ and of $\Lambda$. Then there is $k\in\mathbb N$ with $r^k\bar w\in R$.
--
--   This is the local–global step turning a local integrality statement into a genuine $r$-power multiple inside the Eichler order, for an element of reduced norm equal to the ramified prime $q$. It feeds the construction of descent intertwining data in the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_descentIntertwiningBase_of_moduliTowerWitness_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_descentIntertwiningBase_of_moduliTowerWitness_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd) and its companion.
